# Observation digest of the CPU churn-loop workload: repeatability (R) evidence,
# not accuracy. It is the SHA-256 of the sorted obs.* lines of digests.txt, so
# it does not depend on the build identity, and it must be equal on Apple clang
# and on gcc (Linux). Gate: det.golden, det.two_instances. (The file keeps its
# Phase 1 name so the gate and claim paths do not move.)
#
# Workload (fixture fixtures/cpu/churn-loop.hex, content SHA-256
# dcee7216a88ff2ffaf3e4a2794c3369676fc47493d710f26cd8bbadd19745b77, the 65C02
# CPU under profile none, cost model flat5 (4096-tick run):
#   RAM policy splitmix64, seed 0x0123456789abcdef, load address 0x0200,
#   empty input timeline, tick budget 4096, stop reason budget. The run ends
#   inside PLA of the sixteenth loop iteration (70 + 15 * 255 + 201 ticks):
#   PC 0x021C, X 0x0F, Y 0x08, S 0xFC, hand-derived in fixtures/cpu/churn-loop.s.
# Regenerate (the runner defaults to profile none):
#   build/check/runner/lynx-run --content fixtures/cpu/churn-loop.hex \
#     --load-addr 0200 --ram-policy splitmix64 --ram-seed 0123456789abcdef --profile none \
#     --ticks 4096 --out <scratch dir>
#   and copy the observation_digest value to the last line below.
# Rule: regenerate only when machine behaviour changes on purpose (for example
# a timing refinement of the cost model), after the CPU vectors and the
# hand-derived program checks are green, and give the reason in the commit
# message.
# Phase 5 added obs.state.hex, SHA-256 of the public fieldwise guest-state
# digest. Phase 6 changes its versioned stream from guest-state.v2 to v3 and
# includes the widened, counted timer/audio ring debt and deferred deadline.
# This changes the oracle while leaving the workload, CPU, RAM, and time
# observations unchanged. det.video_sensitivity proves the state stream and
# the newly widened ring debt are both nonvacuous.
4118959d3b07f1b1786e84dfb8f5f584e8e8e493bb8d955cdd019a3df2250342
